1
00:00:02,209 --> 00:00:07,307
The Life Of Muhammad ﷺ Madinan Period Volume 2

2
00:00:07,760 --> 00:00:09,926
By Imam Anwar Al_Awlaki;

3
00:00:10,774 --> 00:00:13,594
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

4
00:00:13,872 --> 00:00:20,601
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرا

5
00:00:21,202 --> 00:00:22,506
Dear Brothers and Sisters,

6
00:00:22,552 --> 00:00:24,402
السلام عليكم ورحمة الله وبركاته

7
00:00:25,137 --> 00:00:32,090
This is our second session of the Madina series, Part Two.

8
00:00:32,764 --> 00:00:38,690
We're talking about the last five years of Rasool Allah ﷺ in Madina.

9
00:00:39,239 --> 00:00:45,793
We talked last session about some events that occurred between Al-Khandaq(ألخندق) and Ghazwa-Tul-Hudaybiyyah(غزوةالحديبيه).

10
00:00:46,301 --> 00:00:51,031
So we carry on now we're in the six year of Hijrah(هجرة)

11
00:00:52,000 --> 00:01:00,761
 and Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر) starts this year with mentioning Ghazwat Zee Qarad(غزوة زي قَرَد) or Ghazwat Al-Ghabaa(غزوة الغابه).

12
00:01:01,285 --> 00:01:06,060
This story has been mentioned by Al-Bukhari(البخاريْ), Muslim(مسلم) Al-Imam Ahmad(الاِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ)

13
00:01:06,097 --> 00:01:10,657
 and also Ibn Is'haqq(اِبْنِ اِسْحَاقْ) mentioned it, so there's various narrations for this story

14
00:01:11,141 --> 00:01:16,477
 and I'll read you the one by Imam Ahmad(اِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ) which is here in Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر)

15
00:01:16,889 --> 00:01:19,674
and I'll translate it as I read it.

16
00:01:20,510 --> 00:01:28,496
 وَقَالَ اِمَامُ اَحْمَدْ حَدَّثَنَا هَاشِمْ اِبْنِ القَاسِمْ حَدَّثّنا عِكْرِمَة بِنْ عَمَّارْ حَدَّ ثَّنِيْ اِيَّاس بِنْ سَلَمَهْ بِنْ اَكْوَعْ عَنْ اَبِيْهِ قَالْ

17
00:01:28,906 --> 00:01:31,534
قَدِّمْنَا الْمَدِيْنَةَ فِيْ زَمَنَ الْحُدَيْبِيَةْ

18
00:01:31,890 --> 00:01:36,191
مَعَ رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم فَخَرَجْتُ اَنَا وَرَبَاْح

19
00:01:36,593 --> 00:01:40,999
غُلَامً النَّبِيْ صلى الله عليه وسلم بِظَهْرِ رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم

20
00:01:41,250 --> 00:01:47,956
وَخَرَجْتُ بِفَرَسِ لِّطَلْحَةَ بِنْ عُبَيْدِ الله ، كُنْتُ اُرِيْدُ اَنْ اُنَدِّيَّه’ مَعَ الْاِبِلْ

21
00:01:48,780 --> 00:01:54,120
Al-Imam Ahmad(اِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ) narrates from Salamah Ibn Akwah(سَلَمَهْ بِنْ اَكْوَعْ) that,

22
00:01:54,663 --> 00:02:00,711
 he along with one of the slaves of Rasool Allah ﷺ, Rabbah(رباح),

23
00:02:01,473 --> 00:02:05,370
they went out of Madina for the camels to graze

24
00:02:06,218 --> 00:02:11,784
and it mentions in, another narration by, I think it's by Al-Waqidee(الواقدي)

25
00:02:12,359 --> 00:02:16,159
that they used to take them first to a place called Bay'yaaz(بياض),

26
00:02:16,843 --> 00:02:19,613
and then that area ran out of pasture.

27
00:02:20,109 --> 00:02:27,950
So, they had to move further on to a place called the Al-Ghaabah(ألغابه), in order, for the camels to graze.

28
00:02:29,037 --> 00:02:35,732
 And Salamah(سلمه), he wasn't with the camels of Rasool Allahﷺ, I mean he wasn't appointed as shepherd,

29
00:02:35,787 --> 00:02:40,835
it was Rabbah(رباح), who was the shepherd but Salamah(سلمه), he went out

30
00:02:41,249 --> 00:02:44,509
because he had the horse of Talha Bin Obaid-Ellah(طلحه بن عبيدالله),

31
00:02:44,589 --> 00:02:47,644
Talha Bin Obaid-Ellah(طلحه بن عبيدالله) is one of Al-Muhajireen(المهاجرين)

32
00:02:47,921 --> 00:02:50,780
one of the 10 who are given the glad tidings of Jannah(جنة).

33
00:02:51,343 --> 00:02:55,417
And Salamah Ibn Akwah(سَلَمَهْ بِنْ اَكْوَعْ) is also a Muhajir(مهاجر), although he's not from Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

34
00:02:56,097 --> 00:02:58,520
 See you have Muhajireen(المهاجرين) and Al-Ansaar(ألأنصار).

35
00:02:58,625 --> 00:02:59,663
Who are Al-Ansaar(ألأنصار).?

36
00:02:59,703 --> 00:03:01,846
Al-Ansaar(ألأنصار) are Al-Aos Wal Khazraj(ألأوس ولخزرج) that's it.

37
00:03:02,080 --> 00:03:03,130
There's no other Ansaar(ألأنصار),

38
00:03:03,223 --> 00:03:05,689
Al-Ansaar(ألأنصار) are two tribes,

39
00:03:06,109 --> 00:03:09,543
two tribes make up Al-Ansaar(ألأنصار), it's only these two tribes.

40
00:03:09,769 --> 00:03:11,812
It is Al-Aos(إلأوس) and Al-Khazraj(ألخزرج)

41
00:03:12,212 --> 00:03:16,527
and these, two tribes our brethren in terms of genealogy,

42
00:03:16,999 --> 00:03:18,128
فِي شجرة النسب

43
00:03:18,783 --> 00:03:23,777
Ya'ani(يعني) they are from the same descendents of Al-Azd(ألأزد)

44
00:03:24,603 --> 00:03:32,063
and Al-Muhajiroon(ألمهاجرون) are everyone else who made Hijrah(هجرة) to Madina

45
00:03:32,582 --> 00:03:36,139
the most important group of Al-Muhajireen(ألمهاجرين), obviously are Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

46
00:03:36,697 --> 00:03:38,508
the tribe of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

47
00:03:39,315 --> 00:03:43,129
So, Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), Umar(عُمَر), Talha Bin Obaid-Ellah(طلحه بن عبيدالله), Saad Ibn Abi Waqas(سعدبن ابي وقاص),

48
00:03:43,474 --> 00:03:46,656
Abu Obaidah Amr Bin Jarrah(ابوعبيدةعمروبن جرَّاح), Saeed Bin Zaid(سعيدبن زيد),

49
00:03:47,292 --> 00:03:51,590
all of these are from the Al-Muhajireen(ألمهاجرين) from Makkah.

50
00:03:51,964 --> 00:03:54,816
But then you had Muhajireen(ألمهاجرين) from other tribes also

51
00:03:55,574 --> 00:03:58,232
you had from Bannu Sulaim(بنو سُلَيْم),

52
00:03:58,619 --> 00:04:01,615
you had from Ghaffar(غِفار) for example Abu Dhar Al-Ghaffari(أبو ذر إلغفاري).

53
00:04:02,078 --> 00:04:05,791
Ghifaar(غفار) are Bedouin tribes in Hijaaz(حجاز),

54
00:04:06,311 --> 00:04:10,021
and Abu Dhar Al-Ghaffari(أبو ذر الغفاري) was Muhajir(مهاجر) from there,

55
00:04:10,061 --> 00:04:15,877
then you have Abu Musa Al-Ashari(أبو موسى ألأشعري) is also considered the Mohajer(مهاجر), he came from Yemen.

56
00:04:16,345 --> 00:04:21,785
So, all of these people who came from outside Madina are called Muhajireen(مهاجرين).

57
00:04:22,578 --> 00:04:28,513
 So, Salamah Ibn Akwah(سَلَمَهْ بِنْ اَكْوَعْ), he is a Mohajer(مهاجر) but he's not from Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

58
00:04:29,248 --> 00:04:35,990
He was serving some of the other Sahabah رضي الله عنهم he was working for Talha Bin Obaid-Ellah(طلحه بن عبيدالله),

59
00:04:36,037 --> 00:04:44,900
he would take out his horse for it, to go out and graze on, the pasture outside of Al-Madina.

60
00:04:45,757 --> 00:04:48,076
And they had to leave early in the day,

61
00:04:48,219 --> 00:04:52,114
another narration it says, that they left before Fajar(فجر) before the first Aadhan(آذان),

62
00:04:52,660 --> 00:04:55,864
so very early on, in the day they had to go out.

63
00:04:56,227 --> 00:05:00,083
Regarding the camels of Rasool Allah ﷺ, they would leave early in the day

64
00:05:00,381 --> 00:05:08,515
and they would come back at the time of Maghrib(مغرب) and then they would milk them and have their dinner.

65
00:05:09,471 --> 00:05:17,116
فَلَمَّا كَانَ بِغَلَسٍ اَغَارَ عَبْدالرحمن بن عُيَيْنَهْ عَلى اِبِلِ رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم

66
00:05:17,438 --> 00:05:23,637
فَقَتَلَ رَاعِيْهَا وَخَرَجَ   يَطْرُدُهَا هُوَ وَاُنَاْس مَعَه’ فِيْ الْخَيْلَ

67
00:05:24,457 --> 00:05:28,820
When it was Ghalas(غلس), Ghalas(غلس) is the time of Fajar(فجر) but it's still dark

68
00:05:29,389 --> 00:05:33,849
Abdur Rahman Ibn Uyaynah(عبدالرحمن إبن عيينه) and these are from the tribe of Ghatafaan(غطافان)

69
00:05:34,222 --> 00:05:41,202
they attacked and they stole the camels of Rasool Allah ﷺ and they killed, the shepherd.

70
00:05:41,748 --> 00:05:46,658
وَخَرَجَ   يَطْرُدُهَا هُوَ وَاُنَاْس مَعَه’ فِيْ الْخَيْلَ فَقُلْتُ: يَا رباح

71
00:05:47,126 --> 00:05:50,964
اُقْعُدْ عَلى هَذَا الْفَرَسْ فَالْحِقْه’ بِطَلْحَه،

72
00:05:51,320 --> 00:05:55,533
وَاَخْبِرْ رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم اَنَّه’ قَدْ اُغِيْرَ عَلى سَرْحِهْ

73
00:05:56,198 --> 00:06:00,409
قَال: وَقُمْتُ عَلى تَلٍّ فَجَعَلْتُ اوَجْهِيْ مِنْ قِبَلِ الْمَدِيْنَةْ ،

74
00:06:00,742 --> 00:06:04,312
ثُمَّ نَادَيْتُ ثَلَاثَ مَرَّاتْ: يَا صُبْاحَاهْ

75
00:06:04,795 --> 00:06:08,170
قال: ثُمَّ اَتْبَعْتُ الْقَوْمَ مَعِيْ سَيْفِيْ وَنَبْلِيْ

76
00:06:08,452 --> 00:06:12,453
فَجَعَلْتُ اَرْمِيْهِمْ وَاَعْقَرْبِهِمْ،وَذَالِكَ حِيْنَ يَكْثُرُ الشَّجَرَ

77
00:06:13,139 --> 00:06:21,393
Salama(سلمه) said: So, I told Rabbah(رباح) take this horse and go back to Madina

78
00:06:21,936 --> 00:06:24,044
and deliver to Talha Bin Obaid-Ellah(طلحه بن عبيدالله)

79
00:06:24,371 --> 00:06:29,877
 and let Rasool Allah ﷺ know that his camels have been taken away.

80
00:06:30,717 --> 00:06:35,908
Salama رضي الله عنه, rather than taking the horse himself, he gave it to Rabbah(رباح),

81
00:06:36,423 --> 00:06:41,255
in order to take it back to Madina, and he depended on his own legs,

82
00:06:41,735 --> 00:06:44,106
he was a very fast runner.

83
00:06:44,742 --> 00:06:47,450
So, he wanted the news to get back to Madina very fast.

84
00:06:47,537 --> 00:06:55,326
 So, he sent Rabbah(رباح) with his horse, but he, himself he climbed over a small mountain or on top of the hill

85
00:06:55,660 --> 00:06:56,455
and then he cried

86
00:06:56,527 --> 00:06:58,728
وَصُبْاحَاهْ، وَصُبْاحَاهْ، وَصُبْاحَاهْ

87
00:06:59,052 --> 00:07:02,953
three times Wa-Subhaa(وَصُبْاحَاه) is the call of emergency

88
00:07:03,185 --> 00:07:07,138
it's like 911 there's something urgent and there's an emergency

89
00:07:07,467 --> 00:07:12,634
that is, what you say and it's especially said, when an army has attacked, you say Wa-Subhaa(وَصُبْاحَاه)

90
00:07:12,811 --> 00:07:18,080
and that is the call that Rasool Allah ﷺ, made

91
00:07:18,514 --> 00:07:22,471
when he wanted to announce to the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) the message.

92
00:07:24,036 --> 00:07:30,221
So when a person calls Wa-Subhaa(وَصُبْاحَاه) people are definitely going to come and listen to him.

93
00:07:31,427 --> 00:07:35,830
Salamah Ibn Akwah(سَلَمَهْ بِنْ اَكْوَعْ) he stood on the mountain on this hill

94
00:07:36,154 --> 00:07:41,082
and he called Wa-Subhaa(وَصُبْاحَاه) and his voice was heard in Madina

95
00:07:41,607 --> 00:07:47,767
and that is when the men were calling and saying when they heard his call,

96
00:07:48,007 --> 00:07:48,814
 they were saying,

97
00:07:48,936 --> 00:07:50,534
يَا خَيْلَ اللهِ الرْكَبِيْ

98
00:07:50,574 --> 00:07:53,181
And this was the first time this slogan was used.

99
00:07:53,221 --> 00:07:54,515
يَا خَيْلَ اللهِ الرْكَبِيْ

100
00:07:54,848 --> 00:07:57,225
O, horses of Allah  ride on.

101
00:07:57,939 --> 00:08:04,286
And the Sahabah(صحابه) responded to the call very fast and they came rushing towards Rasool Allahﷺ,

102
00:08:04,549 --> 00:08:06,451
when they heard the call of Salamah(سلمه).

103
00:08:06,984 --> 00:08:13,596
Now Salamah(سلمه) himself after that he followed Abdur Rahman Ibn Uyaynah(عبدالرحمن إبن عيينه),

104
00:08:14,121 --> 00:08:19,366
and he said; I had with me my sword, and my bow and arrow.

105
00:08:19,925 --> 00:08:21,897
فَجَعَلْتُ اَرْمِيْهِمْ وَاَعْقَرْبِهِمْ

106
00:08:22,362 --> 00:08:26,015
And I would shoot at them and,

107
00:08:26,055 --> 00:08:27,415
وَاَعْقَرْبِهِمْ،

108
00:08:27,659 --> 00:08:32,077
Means I would kill their horses, he would target the horses and kill the horses

109
00:08:32,117 --> 00:08:33,631
وَذَالِكَ حِيْنَ يَكْثُرُ الشَّجَرَ

110
00:08:33,671 --> 00:08:37,454
And I would do that when there would be a lot of trees because he could ambush them.

111
00:08:37,608 --> 00:08:41,919
And he could also take a position of hiding that to protect him.

112
00:08:42,517 --> 00:08:46,263
فَاِذَا رَجَعَ اِلَيَّ فَارِسٌ جَلَسْتُ لَه’ فِيْ اَصْلِ شَّجَرَةْ، ثُمَّ رَمَيْتَ

113
00:08:46,837 --> 00:08:49,341
فَلَا يُقْبِلْ عَلَيَّ فَارِسٌ اِلَّا عَقَرْتُ بِهْ

114
00:08:50,022 --> 00:08:54,309
فَجَعَلْتُ اَرْمِيْهِمْ، وَاَنَا اَقُوْلْ : اَنَا اِبْنِ الْاَكْوَعْ، وَالْيَوْم يَوْمُ الرُّضَّعْ

115
00:08:55,025 --> 00:09:00,238
He said: I would shoot them, when I would be in between trees.

116
00:09:00,570 --> 00:09:03,934
And whenever, one of their horsemen would come back to me

117
00:09:04,243 --> 00:09:08,212
I would hide for him, behind the tree, and I would shoot at him,

118
00:09:08,432 --> 00:09:12,570
while I would call out to them, the Battle Cry of

119
00:09:12,949 --> 00:09:16,430
خُذْهَا وَاَنَا اِبْنِ الْاَكْوَعْ وَالْيَوْم يَوْمُ الرُّضَّعْ

120
00:09:16,941 --> 00:09:19,231
This is a line of poetry that he made.

121
00:09:19,565 --> 00:09:20,854
It says; Take it!

122
00:09:21,332 --> 00:09:27,020
I am Ibn-Al-Aqwa(ابن الاكوع), I'm the son of Al-Aqwa(اكوع), today the wicked will die.

123
00:09:27,060 --> 00:09:27,874
 اَلْيَوْم يَوْمُ الرُّضَّعْ

124
00:09:27,914 --> 00:09:33,565
Means today the wicked will die and he would repeat on this battle cry again and again.

125
00:09:33,919 --> 00:09:36,599
فَاِذَا كُنْتُ فِيْ الشَّجَرْ اَحْرَقْتُهُمْ بِالْنَبَلْ ،

126
00:09:36,872 --> 00:09:42,069
فَاِذَا تَضَايَقَتِ الثَّنَايَا عَلَوْتُ الْجَبَلَ فَرَدَيْتُهُمْ بِالْحِجَارَةْ

127
00:09:42,389 --> 00:09:45,794
فَمَا زَالَ ذَالِكَ شَاْنِيْ وَشَاْنُهُمْ اَتَّبِعُهُمْ وَارْتَجِزْ،

128
00:09:46,018 --> 00:09:47,918
 حَتَّى مَا خَلَقَ اللهُ شَيْئاً

129
00:09:48,145 --> 00:09:51,852
مِنْ ظَهَرِ رسول االه صلى الله عليه وسلم اِلَّا خَلَّفْتَه’ وَرَاَءْ ظَهْرِيْ

130
00:09:52,321 --> 00:09:54,958
He said: When I would be in the trees,

131
00:09:55,061 --> 00:09:56,430
 اَحْرَقْتُهُمْ بِالْنَبَلْ

132
00:09:56,630 --> 00:09:59,041
I would burn them with my arrows.

133
00:09:59,422 --> 00:10:05,041
And if we come through mountain passes narrow trails in the mountain,

134
00:10:05,461 --> 00:10:08,935
I would climb on top of them and throw them with rocks.

135
00:10:09,145 --> 00:10:12,443
So, Salama Ibn Al-Akwa رضي الله عنه was driving these men crazy.

136
00:10:12,536 --> 00:10:17,096
I mean, he's alone and he's fighting this entire group of men.

137
00:10:17,583 --> 00:10:21,104
So, first of all, he's alone and they are a large group.

138
00:10:21,393 --> 00:10:25,395
Number two, he was on foot and they were on horseback.

139
00:10:26,167 --> 00:10:31,937
But Salamah(سلمه) was courageous and he was fast, and he was a good Archer.

140
00:10:32,337 --> 00:10:35,180
 And, the most important of all, he was a Mo'min(مؤمن).

141
00:10:36,661 --> 00:10:40,783
He said: Everything that they have taken away, I left it behind my back.

142
00:10:40,850 --> 00:10:43,802
These men were running away from Salamah(سلمه)

143
00:10:44,216 --> 00:10:48,383
and to make themselves light and faster in running away from him.

144
00:10:48,918 --> 00:10:54,079
They left behind the camels and then they started in fact, leaving behind some of their own belongings.

145
00:10:54,676 --> 00:11:02,602
It says in one narration that they left behind them 30 spears and 30 cloaks, Burad(بُرد)

146
00:11:03,122 --> 00:11:05,804
 they had to leave all this behind them, to lighten their weight

147
00:11:05,869 --> 00:11:08,814
and whenever, Salamah(سلمه) would come across something, they would leave

148
00:11:08,931 --> 00:11:12,798
he would put some stones on top of it to mark its location.

149
00:11:13,786 --> 00:11:19,437
حَتَّى إِذَا امْتَدْ الضُّحَى أَتَاهُمْ عُيَيْنَة بِنْ بَدْر اَلْفَزَارِيْ مَدَدَا لَّهُمْ

150
00:11:20,366 --> 00:11:25,383
وَهُمْ فِيْ ثَنِيَّةٍ ضَيِّقَةْ ، ثُمَّ عَلَوْتُ الْجَبَلْ ، فَأَنَا فَوْقَهُمْ

151
00:11:26,233 --> 00:11:28,413
فَقَالَ عُيَيْنَةْ : مَا هَذَا الَّذِيْ أَرَى ؟

152
00:11:28,560 --> 00:11:30,453
قَالُوْا : لَقِيْنَا مِنْ هَذَا الْبَرْحْ

153
00:11:30,800 --> 00:11:37,977
مَا فَارَقَنَا بِسَحَرٍ حَتَّى الْآنْ ، وَأَخَذَ كُلَّ شَيْءٍ فِيْ أَيْدِيْنَا وَجَعَلَه’ وَرَاءَ ظَهْرِهْ

154
00:11:38,343 --> 00:11:44,987
فَقَالَ عُيَيْنَةْ : لَوْلَا أَنَّ هَذَا يَرَى أَنَّ وَرَاَءَهْ طَلَبَا لَّقَدْ تَرَكَكُمْ ، لِيَقُمْ إِلَيْهِ نَفَرُ مِّنْكُمْ

155
00:11:45,415 --> 00:11:49,731
And then, they received reinforcements from Uyayena Bin Badar Al-Fizaari(عيينة بن بدر ألفزاري)

156
00:11:50,191 --> 00:11:54,511
he came to them and they were in a narrow mountain pass.

157
00:11:54,964 --> 00:11:56,511
So, I climbed on top of them.

158
00:11:56,711 --> 00:11:58,793
And then Uyeyena(عيينة) said: What is this that I see?

159
00:11:59,060 --> 00:12:02,942
They said, We have seen such a difficult time from this man.

160
00:12:03,333 --> 00:12:08,430
And then they said: He has not left us since early in the day, until this moment

161
00:12:08,872 --> 00:12:11,525
and he has taken everything away from us,

162
00:12:12,336 --> 00:12:18,525
Uyeyena(عيينة) told them, if this man sees that you are pursuing him, he would not follow you.

163
00:12:18,878 --> 00:12:20,934
Meaning why are you leaving them alone?

164
00:12:21,098 --> 00:12:26,694
You are the ones who are giving him, that chance but pursue him and he will leave you alone.

165
00:12:27,033 --> 00:12:37,564
So, four of them at the command of Uyeyena(عيينة) started climbing up the mountain to go up to Salamahرضي الله عنه.

166
00:12:38,152 --> 00:12:43,797
So, they started climbing the mountain, until they were in his voice range, he said,

167
00:12:44,326 --> 00:12:46,729
فَلَمَّا أَسْمَعْتَهُمْ الصَوْتَ قُلْتَ : أَتَعْرِفُوْنَنِيْ ؟

168
00:12:47,023 --> 00:12:49,649
قَالُوْا : وَمَنْ أَنْت ؟ قُلْتُ : أَنَا اِبْنُ الْأَكْوَعْ

169
00:12:49,889 --> 00:12:56,143
وَالَّذِيْ كَرَّمَ وَجْهِ محمد لَا يَطْلُبْنِيْ رَجُلٌ مِّنْكُمْ فَيُدْرِكْنِيْ وَلَا أَطْلُبُهْ فَيَفُوْتَنِيْ

170
00:12:57,065 --> 00:12:59,022
فَقَالَ رَجُلُ مِّنْهُمْ  اَنَ أَظُنْ

171
00:12:59,820 --> 00:13:02,199
When they were in his voice, he said: You know who I am?

172
00:13:02,542 --> 00:13:05,921
They said: No. He said: I am the son of Al-Aqwa(الأكوع),

173
00:13:06,565 --> 00:13:13,162
in the name of the one, who has honored the face of Muhammadﷺ

174
00:13:13,934 --> 00:13:18,866
none of you would follow me and reach me

175
00:13:19,175 --> 00:13:25,401
and none of you, whom I follow will escape me, if you try to chase me.

176
00:13:25,827 --> 00:13:28,761
If you try to get me, you won't be able to

177
00:13:29,321 --> 00:13:31,924
but if I pursue you I would hunt you down.

178
00:13:32,341 --> 00:13:33,877
One of them said: I think he's right.

179
00:13:34,334 --> 00:13:36,103
And then they descended.

180
00:13:37,228 --> 00:13:42,743
قَالَ : فَمَا بَرِحْتُ مَقْعَدِيْ ذَلِكَ حَتَّى نَظَرْتُ إِلَى فَوَارِسَ رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم

181
00:13:43,210 --> 00:13:48,183
At that time I started seeing the Knights of Rasool Allah ﷺ approaching.

182
00:13:48,617 --> 00:13:49,832
يَتَّخَلَّلُوْنَ الشَّجَرَ

183
00:13:49,899 --> 00:13:51,939
I could see them between the trees.

184
00:13:52,721 --> 00:13:54,637
وَإِذَا أَوَّلُهُمْ اَلْأَخْرَمْ اَلْأَسْدِيْ

185
00:13:54,926 --> 00:13:59,719
The first among them was Akhram Al-Asdi(اَلأخْرم الأسدي) and following him was Abu Qatada(ابوقتادة),

186
00:14:00,059 --> 00:14:04,156
the Faris(فارس) of Rasool Allah ﷺ the knight of Rasool Ullah.

187
00:14:04,556 --> 00:14:07,599
وَعَلى أِثْرِ أَبِيْ قَتَادَةْ اَلْمِقْدَادْ بِنْ اَلْأَسْوَدْ

188
00:14:07,679 --> 00:14:11,922
and after Abu Qatada(ابوقتادة) was Al-Miqdad Ibn Al-Aswad(ألمقداد إبن الأسود).

189
00:14:12,356 --> 00:14:14,359
فَوَلَّى الْمُشْرِكُوْنَ  مُدْبِرِيْنَ

190
00:14:14,594 --> 00:14:18,379
When the polytheist saw that, they ran away.

191
00:14:18,891 --> 00:14:25,807
وَأَنْزِلُ مِنَّ الْجَبَلِ فَآخَذُ عَنَانَ فَرَسِهْ ، فَقُلْتُ : يَا أَخْرَمْ اَنْذِرِ الْقَوْمْ

192
00:14:25,944 --> 00:14:29,887
يَعْنِيْ اِحْذَرْهُمْ - فَإِنِّيْ لَا آمَنْ مِنْ أَنْ يَقْتَطِعُوْكَ ،

193
00:14:30,340 --> 00:14:34,062
فَاتَّئِدْ حتَىَّ يَلْحِقَ رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم وَأَصْحَابُهْ

194
00:14:34,887 --> 00:14:38,781
The first as we said was Akhram Al-Asdi(اَلأخْرم الأسدي), so I came down

195
00:14:39,121 --> 00:14:42,750
and I held on to the reins of his horse

196
00:14:43,304 --> 00:14:47,667
and I told him: O Akhram( أخرم) Be careful from them!

197
00:14:48,161 --> 00:14:50,697
Because I fear that they will cut you off,

198
00:14:51,154 --> 00:14:55,266
because Al-Akhram( الأخرم) was ahead of the rest and he was alone.

199
00:14:55,701 --> 00:15:01,241
And Salamah(سلمه) wanted to warn him that, if you carry on pursuing the Kuffar(كفار) alone

200
00:15:01,281 --> 00:15:06,703
 and you don't wait for the rest of the Muslims to follow they would cut you off and surround you.

201
00:15:07,567 --> 00:15:10,649
What was the response of Akhram Al-Asdi(اَلأخْرم الأسدي) he said,

202
00:15:11,029 --> 00:15:15,861
قَالَ يَا سَلَمة ، إِنْ كُنْتَ تُؤْمِنْ بِاللهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرْ

203
00:15:16,559 --> 00:15:23,047
وَتَعْلَمْ أَنَّ الْجَنَّةَ حَقّْ وَالنَّارْ حَقّْ فَلَا تَحُلْ بَيْنِيْ وَبَيْنَ الشَّهَادَةْ

204
00:15:23,886 --> 00:15:28,253
He said: O Salamah(سلمه), if you believe in Allah and the last day

205
00:15:28,495 --> 00:15:32,904
and you believe that Jannah(جنة) is true, and Naar(النار) is true

206
00:15:33,213 --> 00:15:37,295
then don't stand between me and martyrdom, Allah-Ho-Akbar(الله اكبر).

207
00:15:37,964 --> 00:15:43,453
Look at the love that Al-Akhram( الأخرم) had for meeting Allahعَزّوجَلّ

208
00:15:43,902 --> 00:15:46,821
he wanted to meet Allahعَزّوجَلّ as a Shaheed(شهيد).

209
00:15:47,487 --> 00:15:48,360
Salamah(سلمه) said;

210
00:15:48,456 --> 00:15:50,130
فَخَلَّيْتُ عَنَّانَ فَرَسِهْ

211
00:15:50,407 --> 00:15:51,430
I let him go.

212
00:15:51,715 --> 00:15:55,574
فَيَلْحِقْ بِعَبْدُ الرحمن بن عيينة وَيَعْطِفُ عَلَيْهِ عبد الرحمن

213
00:15:55,614 --> 00:15:57,699
 So, he pursued Abdur Rahman Ibn Uyeyena(عبدالرحمن إبن عيينه),

214
00:15:57,912 --> 00:16:00,072
and Uyeyena(عيينه) turned around, to face him.

215
00:16:00,279 --> 00:16:01,705
 فَاخْتَلَفَا طَعْنَتَيْنَ

216
00:16:01,926 --> 00:16:03,873
each one of them stab the other

217
00:16:04,596 --> 00:16:06,276
فَعَقْرَ الْأخرم بِعَبْدُ الرحمن

218
00:16:06,810 --> 00:16:10,543
Al-Akhram(الأخرم) stabbed the horse of Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن)

219
00:16:10,663 --> 00:16:13,528
but Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن) stabbed him and killed him,

220
00:16:13,934 --> 00:16:18,906
so now the horse of Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن) was killed and Al-Akhram( الأخرم) was killed.

221
00:16:19,246 --> 00:16:23,574
So Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن) now took over the horse of Al-Akhram( الأخرم).

222
00:16:24,728 --> 00:16:30,533
فَتَحَوَّلَ عَبْد الرحمن عَلَى فَرَسِ الْأَخْرَم ، فَيَلْحَقْ أَبُوْ قَتَادَةْ بِعَبْدُ الرحمن فَاخْتَلَفَا طَعْنَتَيْنَ

223
00:16:30,783 --> 00:16:36,370
فَعُقِرَة بِي اَبِي قَتَادَة وَقَتَلَه أَبُوْ قَتَاَدَةْ ، وَتَحَوَّلَ أَبُوْ قَتَادَةْ عَلَى فَرَسِ الْأَخْرَمْ

224
00:16:36,451 --> 00:16:39,817
Now, the opposite happened Abu Qatadah(ابوقتادة) attacked, Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن)

225
00:16:40,118 --> 00:16:48,390
 and in this case it was Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن), who killed the horse, stabbed at the horse of Abu Qatadah(ابوقتادة) and killed it.

226
00:16:48,751 --> 00:16:51,442
While the Abu Qatadah(ابوقتادة) stabbed Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن) and killed him

227
00:16:51,754 --> 00:16:58,008
so now he took over the horse that Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن) had which is originally the horse of Al-Akhram( الأخرم).

228
00:16:59,487 --> 00:17:02,079
 ثُمَّ إِنِّيْ خَرَجْتُ أَعْدُوْ فِيْ أَثْرِ الْقَوْمَ

229
00:17:02,399 --> 00:17:07,263
حَتَّى مَا أَرَى مِنْ غُبَارِ صَحَابَةِ النَّبِيْ صلى الله عليه وسلم شَيْئَا

230
00:17:07,596 --> 00:17:09,397
This is amazing here, Salamah(سلمه) said;

231
00:17:09,464 --> 00:17:13,099
 And now I started running after the enemies of Allah

232
00:17:13,503 --> 00:17:18,326
until, I could not see from the dust of the companions of Rasool Ullah a thing.

233
00:17:18,942 --> 00:17:24,633
All of the horsemen of Rasool Allah ﷺ were now behind Salamah(سلمه) while Salamah(سلمه) was running on foot.

234
00:17:25,533 --> 00:17:30,688
وَيُعْرِضُوْنَ قَبْلَ غَيْبُوْبَةِ الشَّمْسَ إِلَى شِعْبٍ فِيْهِ مَاءْ يُقَالُ لَه ذُوْ قَرَدْ

235
00:17:31,132 --> 00:17:35,636
فَأَرَادُوْا أَنْ يَشْرَبُوْا مِنْه’ ، فَأَبْصَرُوْنِيْ أَعْدُوْ وَرَاءَهُمْ فَعَطَفُوْا عَنْه’

236
00:17:36,233 --> 00:17:39,737
So, now it was almost Maghrib(مغرب) time, sunset

237
00:17:40,092 --> 00:17:46,177
and they reached to a valley that had some water in it.

238
00:17:46,554 --> 00:17:50,019
It's called Zou Qarad(ذوقرد) and they wanted to drink from that water

239
00:17:50,059 --> 00:17:54,291
 but when they saw me running after them, pursuing them they left it

240
00:17:54,751 --> 00:17:57,223
 and they started running up the hills.

241
00:17:57,893 --> 00:18:00,404
وَغَرَبَتِ الشَّمْسَ ، وَأَلْحَقُ رَجُلْ فَأَرْمِيْهَ

242
00:18:00,851 --> 00:18:07,145
And now the sun has set, so I followed one of them and I struck him, with an arrow and I told him,

243
00:18:07,568 --> 00:18:10,435
خُذْهَا وَاَنَا اِبْنِ الْاَكْوَعْ وَالْيَوْم يَوْمُ الرُّضَّعْ

244
00:18:10,749 --> 00:18:16,406
So, he repeated, his battle cry, take it, I am the son of Al-Aqwa(الأكوع),

245
00:18:16,708 --> 00:18:19,475
today the wicked will die, whay did that man say?

246
00:18:19,545 --> 00:18:21,553
فَقَالَ : يَا ثَكْلَ أُمَّ أَكْوَعْ بُكْرَةْ

247
00:18:21,987 --> 00:18:27,824
He said: Woe to your mother, are you the Aqwa(أكوع) of this morning.?

248
00:18:28,360 --> 00:18:31,992
I mean are you the same man who has been following us since the beginning of the day.?

249
00:18:32,155 --> 00:18:32,677
فَقُلْتَ : نَعْمَ

250
00:18:32,717 --> 00:18:33,436
I said yes,

251
00:18:33,735 --> 00:18:34,761
أَيّ عَدُّوَّ نَفْسَهْ

252
00:18:34,935 --> 00:18:36,031
You enemy of yourself!

253
00:18:36,329 --> 00:18:41,663
وَكَانَ الَّذِيْ رَمَيْتَه’ بُكْرَةْ وَأَتْبَعْتَه’ سَهْمًا آخَرْ فَعَلِقَ بِهْ سَهْمَانْ

254
00:18:42,110 --> 00:18:46,908
And this happened to be a man whom I have already struck with an arrow in the morning,

255
00:18:47,184 --> 00:18:49,471
so now he had two arrows sticking out of him.

256
00:18:50,592 --> 00:18:53,535
وَيَخْلُفُوْنَ فَرَسَيْنَ فَجِئْتُ بِهِمَا أَسُوْقَهُمَا

257
00:18:53,848 --> 00:18:58,081
إِلَى رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم وَهُوَ عَلَى الْمَاءْ اَلَّذِيْ أَجْلَيْتُهُمْ عَنْه

258
00:18:58,494 --> 00:19:02,533
ذُوْ قَرَدْ - وَإِذَا بِنَبِيُ الله صلى الله عليه وسلم فِيْ خَمْس مِائَةْ

259
00:19:03,103 --> 00:19:06,621
وَإِذَا بِلَالْ قَدْ نَحَرَ جَزُوْرَا مِمَّا خَلَّفْتَ ،

260
00:19:06,854 --> 00:19:10,660
فَهُوَ يَشْوِيْ لِرَسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم مِنْ كَبدِهَا وَسَنَامِهَا

261
00:19:11,027 --> 00:19:14,531
He said: They left behind them two horses, so I took them over

262
00:19:14,867 --> 00:19:17,802
and now I went back to Rasool Allah ﷺ

263
00:19:18,113 --> 00:19:22,828
and I found them sitting on the same well or water

264
00:19:23,184 --> 00:19:26,489
that was in this valley which the Mushrikeen(مشركين) wanted to drink from

265
00:19:26,703 --> 00:19:29,365
and I found Rasool Allah ﷺ with 500 men

266
00:19:29,619 --> 00:19:34,518
and Bilal(بلال) was slaughtering for them one of the camels that I have left behind me

267
00:19:34,798 --> 00:19:40,251
and he was roasting part of its liver and it's meaning

268
00:19:40,315 --> 00:19:41,922
 كَبدِهَا وَسَنَامِهَا

269
00:19:42,684 --> 00:19:46,781
And he was roasting for them from this camel

270
00:19:47,229 --> 00:19:50,060
and I came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and told him.

271
00:19:50,125 --> 00:19:58,348
يا رسول الله ، خَلِّنِيْ فَأَنْتَخِبُ مِنْ أَصْحَابِكَ مِائَةْ ، فَآخَذْ عَلَى الْكُفَّارِ بِالْعَشْوَةْ ، فَلَا يَبْقَى مِنْهُمْ مُخْبِرْ إِلَّا قَتَلْتَه

272
00:19:58,556 --> 00:20:02,435
O Rasool Ullah, let me choose 100 from amongst your men

273
00:20:02,763 --> 00:20:07,626
and I would pursue with them, the Kuffar(كفار), until we'll leave none of them alive.

274
00:20:08,167 --> 00:20:10,335
فَقَالَ : " أَكُنْتَ فَاعِلٍا ذَلِكَ يَا سَلَمْةَ ؟

275
00:20:10,535 --> 00:20:12,254
would you do so, O Salamah(سلمه).

276
00:20:12,501 --> 00:20:12,995
قُلْتُ : نَعَمْ

277
00:20:13,055 --> 00:20:13,934
I said: Yes.

278
00:20:14,129 --> 00:20:15,002
وَالَّذِيْ أَكْرَمَكْ

279
00:20:15,042 --> 00:20:17,038
In the name of Allah, who has honored you,

280
00:20:17,342 --> 00:20:22,226
Rasool Allah ﷺ laughed, until I saw his teeth from the light of the fire.

281
00:20:22,887 --> 00:20:26,890
ثُمَّ قَالْ : إِنَّهُمْ يَقْرَوْنَ الْآنْ بِأَرْضِ غَطَفَان

282
00:20:27,139 --> 00:20:30,940
Now, they are already being fed in the land of Ghatafaan(غطفان).

283
00:20:31,321 --> 00:20:32,788
A man came from Ghatafaan(غطفان) and said:

284
00:20:32,828 --> 00:20:36,215
مَرُّوْا عَلَى فُلَانْ الغطفاني، فَنَحْرَ لَهُمْ جَزُوْرًا

285
00:20:36,637 --> 00:20:41,452
They passed by certain men from Ghatafaan(غطفان), so he slaughtered for them a camel

286
00:20:41,731 --> 00:20:46,797
فَلَمَّا أَخَذُوْا يَكْشَطُوْنَ جِلْدَهَا رَأَوْا غَبَرَةْ ، فَتَرَكُوْهَا وَخَرَجُوْا هِرَابًا

287
00:20:46,996 --> 00:20:50,479
And when they started skinning the camel,

288
00:20:50,708 --> 00:20:54,187
they saw some dust, so they left it and ran away

289
00:20:54,324 --> 00:20:56,572
they thought that this is Rasool Allah ﷺ and his companions

290
00:20:56,633 --> 00:20:59,337
so they didn't even enjoy their meal.

291
00:20:59,830 --> 00:21:03,904
When it was morning of the next day, Rasool Allah ﷺ said,

292
00:21:04,357 --> 00:21:10,236
خَيْرُ فُرْسَانِنَا الْيَوْم أبو قتادة ، وَخَيْرُ رَجَّالَتِنَا سَلَمَة

293
00:21:10,512 --> 00:21:14,093
The best of our horseman today, is Abu Qatadah(ابوقتادة)

294
00:21:14,434 --> 00:21:17,376
and the best of our foot soldiers is Salamah(سلمه).

295
00:21:18,731 --> 00:21:22,000
فَأَعْطَانِيْ رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم سَهْمٌ الفَارِسْ وَالرَاجُلْ جَمِيْعَا

296
00:21:22,639 --> 00:21:29,510
Rasool Allah ﷺ gave me spoils of war equal to that of a knight and a foot soldier together.

297
00:21:29,896 --> 00:21:33,745
ثُمَّ أَرْدَفَنِيْ وَرَاءَهُ عَلَى الْعَضْبَاءْ رَاجِعِيْنَ إِلَى الْمَدِيْنَةَ

298
00:21:34,025 --> 00:21:37,751
And he had me ride with him on his Camel, Al-Adhba'a(ألعضباء),

299
00:21:38,108 --> 00:21:40,154
until when we were going back to Madina.

300
00:21:40,387 --> 00:21:43,253
فَلَمَّا كَانَ بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَهُمْ قَرِيْبَ مِنْ ضَحْوَةْ

301
00:21:44,189 --> 00:21:47,379
When we were close to Al-Madina.

302
00:21:48,056 --> 00:21:52,426
وَفِي الْقَوْمِ رَجُلٌ مِنْ اَلْأَنْصَارْ كَانَ لَا يُسْبَقْ جَعَلَ يُنَادِيْ

303
00:21:53,395 --> 00:21:56,508
فَلَمَّا كَانَ بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَهُمْ قَرِيْبَ مِنْ ضَحْوَةْ

304
00:21:56,871 --> 00:22:01,091
When we were close to Al-Madina and Dhahwa(ضَحْوَةْ) is

305
00:22:01,728 --> 00:22:06,065
something like around half a day distance or something like that.

306
00:22:06,494 --> 00:22:08,982
وَفِي الْقَوْمِ رَجُلٌ مِنْ اَلْأَنْصَارْ كَانَ لَا يُسْبَقْ

307
00:22:09,410 --> 00:22:17,176
And amongst us, was a man from an Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار), who was not defeated in racing

308
00:22:17,535 --> 00:22:20,101
فَجَعَلَ يُنَادِيْ : هَلْ مِنْ مُسَابِقْ

309
00:22:20,712 --> 00:22:24,034
He would call out, Is there anyone who would race me.?

310
00:22:24,554 --> 00:22:27,354
This was the best among Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار), fast runner.

311
00:22:27,991 --> 00:22:30,375
أَلَا رَجُلٌ يُسَابِقْ إِلَى الْمَدِيْنَةْ

312
00:22:30,479 --> 00:22:34,180
Is there anyone who would race me, to Madina?

313
00:22:34,488 --> 00:22:36,510
And we kept on repeating that again and again,

314
00:22:37,238 --> 00:22:39,804
while I am behind Rasool Allah ﷺ so I told him.

315
00:22:40,194 --> 00:22:43,152
أَمَّا تُكْرِمُ كَرِيْمًا وَلَا تَهَابُ شَرِيْفًا

316
00:22:43,501 --> 00:22:49,191
Don't you honor, the honorable and Don't you fear the noble.

317
00:22:49,517 --> 00:22:54,114
He said: No except Rasool Allah ﷺ, What's Salamah(سلمه) meant by that is

318
00:22:54,408 --> 00:22:57,397
I mean, you've been challenging us too much.

319
00:22:57,657 --> 00:23:04,380
Don't you have respect for anyone, obviously he was joking with this Ansaari(اَنصاري)

320
00:23:04,923 --> 00:23:07,751
and saying don't you respect the noble or fear the powerful

321
00:23:08,220 --> 00:23:15,202
so this man said: No, except Rasool Allahﷺ this is the only one, whom I would not challenge.

322
00:23:15,762 --> 00:23:24,357
Tayyab(طيب), when he said that and Salama Ibn Aqwaرضي الله عنه has been running the entire day before

323
00:23:24,743 --> 00:23:29,870
 but this challenge was too much for him, to pass on

324
00:23:29,963 --> 00:23:33,318
because this man has been repeating it again and again.

325
00:23:34,011 --> 00:23:34,778
So, he said;

326
00:23:34,892 --> 00:23:40,453
يا رسول الله ، بِأَبِيْ أَنْتَ وَأُمِّيْ ، خَلِّنِيْ فَلَأُسَابِقَ الرَّجُلْ . قَالَ : إِنْ شِئْتَ

327
00:23:41,136 --> 00:23:42,778
So I said O Messenger of Allah

328
00:23:43,649 --> 00:23:46,908
May my father and mother be sacrifice for you.

329
00:23:46,988 --> 00:23:49,914
Let me race this man.

330
00:23:50,373 --> 00:23:50,928
قَالَ : إِنْ شِئْتَ

331
00:23:50,975 --> 00:23:51,771
If you want.

332
00:23:52,268 --> 00:23:59,366
قُلْتَ : اَذْهَبْ إِلَيْكَ . فَطَفَرَ عَنْ رَاحِلَتِهْ وَثَنَيْتُ رِجْلِيْ فَطَفَرْتُ عَنْ النَّاقَةْ

333
00:24:00,225 --> 00:24:05,551
ثُمَّ إِنِّيْ رَبَطْتُّ عَلَيْهِ شَرَفًا أَوْ شَرْفَيْنَ ، يَعْنِيْ اِسْتَبْقَيْتَ مِنْ نَفْسِيْ

334
00:24:05,876 --> 00:24:12,895
ثُمَّ إِنِّيْ عَدَوْتُ حَتَّى أَلْحَقَّهْ ، فَأَصُكْ بَيْنَ كَتِفَيْهِ بِيَدِيْ ، قُلْتَ : سَبَقْتُكَ وَالله

335
00:24:13,246 --> 00:24:18,715
أَوْ كَلِمَةْ نَحْوَهَا . قَالَ : فَضَحِكْ وَقَالَ : إِنْ أَظُنْ . حَتَّى قَدِمْنَا الْمَدِيْنَةْ

336
00:24:19,704 --> 00:24:26,300
So, he said: I'll come to you and at this, he jumped off his mount

337
00:24:26,786 --> 00:24:30,312
 and I bent my leg and jumped down from the camel

338
00:24:30,871 --> 00:24:35,380
and then Salama رضي الله عنه let the man get the head of him,

339
00:24:36,135 --> 00:24:40,919
while he was holding himself back because he said

340
00:24:40,977 --> 00:24:42,185
اِسْتَبْقَيْ نَفْسِيْ

341
00:24:42,652 --> 00:24:50,253
He wanted to preserve his breath, so he was allowing this man to be ahead of him for a particular distance,

342
00:24:50,313 --> 00:24:54,515
 until we got close to Madina, then I ran hard

343
00:24:55,184 --> 00:25:02,491
and when I was behind him, I slapped him between his shoulders with my hand

344
00:25:02,965 --> 00:25:06,687
and told him; I beat you in the name of Allah,

345
00:25:07,324 --> 00:25:11,125
the man laughed and said: I agreed, so he went into Madina.

346
00:25:11,714 --> 00:25:16,186
So, for the entire race this Ansari(اَنصاري) was ahead of Salamah(سلمه)

347
00:25:16,621 --> 00:25:21,297
but when they were close to Madina, Salamah(سلمه) picked up speed

348
00:25:21,777 --> 00:25:24,390
and then when he was passing next to the Ansari(اَنصاري)

349
00:25:24,870 --> 00:25:29,895
he patted him between his shoulders and told him I beat you by the name of Allah,

350
00:25:30,215 --> 00:25:30,715
 the man said;

351
00:25:30,755 --> 00:25:31,305
إِنْ أَظُنْ

352
00:25:31,408 --> 00:25:32,184
You are right.

353
00:25:33,059 --> 00:25:36,406
And this was the fastest runner among Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار)

354
00:25:36,808 --> 00:25:40,929
but nobody can beat Salama Ibn Aqwa رضي الله عنه.

355
00:25:41,186 --> 00:25:47,859
This is the story of Ghazwat Zee Qarad(غزوة زي قَرَد) or what is called also Ghazwat Al-Ghabaa(غزوة الغابه).

356
00:25:48,168 --> 00:25:56,113
And then Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر) talks here about the camel of Rasool Allah ﷺ Al-Adhba'a(ألعضباء)

357
00:25:56,561 --> 00:26:00,171
 and the story of the Camel Al-Adhba'a(ألعضباء) because here we mentioned

358
00:26:00,495 --> 00:26:06,740
that Rasool Allah ﷺ was riding on Al-Adbaa(ألعضباء) and he had Salama رضي الله عنه ride with him.

359
00:26:06,820 --> 00:26:09,639
 So, what's the story of Al-Adhba'a(ألعضباء)?

360
00:26:10,199 --> 00:26:12,046
Al-Adhba'a(ألعضباء) was a very fast Camel

361
00:26:12,496 --> 00:26:15,964
and it belongs to a man from Banni Aqeel(بني عقيل)

362
00:26:16,322 --> 00:26:20,592
so how did it end up in the hands of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

363
00:26:20,984 --> 00:26:26,077
This Hadith(حديث) is narrated by Imam Ahmad Bin Hanbal رضي الله عنه, it says that;

364
00:26:26,155 --> 00:26:30,171
كَانَتِ الْعَضْبَاءْ :لِرَجُلٍ مِنْ بَنِيْ عَقِيْلْ ، وَكَانَتْ مِنْ سَوَابِقِ الْحَاج

365
00:26:30,805 --> 00:26:35,268
Al-Adhba'a(ألعضباء) belong to a man from Banni Aqeel(بني عقيل) and it was a racing camel

366
00:26:35,789 --> 00:26:37,243
مِنْ سَوَابِقِ الْحَاج

367
00:26:37,649 --> 00:26:42,285
It was very fast Camel, it was Hajj(حج) racing camel.

368
00:26:42,742 --> 00:26:48,917
This man was taken captive by the Muslims along with his camel.

369
00:26:49,310 --> 00:26:53,497
Rasool Allah ﷺ passed by him, when he was tied up

370
00:26:54,103 --> 00:26:57,356
and Rasool Allah ﷺ was riding on a donkey then

371
00:26:57,747 --> 00:27:00,578
so the man called out to Muhammadﷺ and said;

372
00:27:00,696 --> 00:27:04,881
يَا محمد ، عَلَامَ تَأْخُذُوْنِيْ وَتَأْخُذُوْنِ سَابِقَةِ الْحَاجْ

373
00:27:05,289 --> 00:27:09,122
Why did you take me and take the Al-Adhba'a(ألعضباء),

374
00:27:09,461 --> 00:27:11,715
the racing camel of Hajj(حَجْ).

375
00:27:12,461 --> 00:27:15,997
This man from Banni Aqeel(بني عقيل) it is protesting, Why was he arrested?

376
00:27:16,404 --> 00:27:17,736
Why was he taken captive?

377
00:27:18,200 --> 00:27:21,246
He was traveling somewhere in Arabia and the Sahabah(صحابه) saw him

378
00:27:21,663 --> 00:27:25,747
and they captured him, and brought him to Madina and they tie him up.

379
00:27:26,226 --> 00:27:31,434
So, now when he saw Muhammadﷺ passing by him, he said: Why have you taken me?

380
00:27:32,293 --> 00:27:34,050
Rasool Allah ﷺ responded back

381
00:27:34,130 --> 00:27:36,755
and this man, the reason why, he was protesting

382
00:27:36,914 --> 00:27:40,907
is because his particular tribe were not in a state of war with the Muslims,

383
00:27:40,987 --> 00:27:44,331
 they were not fighting the Muslims, there was no battle between them and the Muslim.

384
00:27:44,448 --> 00:27:45,653
So, why was I taken.

385
00:27:45,971 --> 00:27:48,771
Rasool Allah ﷺ answered back and told him,

386
00:27:49,005 --> 00:27:52,780
نَأْخُذُكَ بِجَرِيْرَةِ حُلَفَائِكَ ثَقِيْفَ

387
00:27:53,068 --> 00:27:57,962
We take you because of the fault of your allies Thaqeef(ثقيف).

388
00:27:58,992 --> 00:28:03,308
Now Thaqeef(ثقيف) were in war with Rasool Allah ﷺ,

389
00:28:04,078 --> 00:28:08,441
up until that moment there were no battles between the Muslims and Thaqeef(ثقيف)

390
00:28:08,475 --> 00:28:14,095
 but Thaqeef(ثقيف) were supportive of Quraish(قريش) in their efforts and they were against Islam in general

391
00:28:14,555 --> 00:28:18,131
 and we know the story of Rasool Allah ﷺ, when he went to At-Taef(اَلطَّائِف)

392
00:28:18,292 --> 00:28:20,751
because Thaqeef(ثقيف) are the tribe that lives in At-Taef(اَلطَّائِف)

393
00:28:21,245 --> 00:28:23,889
and we know what happened to Rasool Allah ﷺ in that journey.

394
00:28:24,292 --> 00:28:31,762
So Rasool Allah ﷺ said: We have taken captive because of the actions of your allies Thaqeef(ثقيف).

395
00:28:32,530 --> 00:28:38,530
 At that particular moment, Thaqeef(ثقيف) have taken two Muslims as captives, you see.

396
00:28:39,129 --> 00:28:45,649
So, now Rasool Allah ﷺ has taken this man as captive as a revenge against Thaqeef(ثقيف)

397
00:28:45,772 --> 00:28:48,971
even though, this man himself was not from Thaqeef(ثقيف)

398
00:28:49,026 --> 00:28:52,386
but he was from Banni Aqeel(بني عقيل), the allies of Thaqeef(ثقيف).

399
00:28:53,801 --> 00:28:56,268
So, what did the man say, he said: I'm a Muslim.

400
00:28:56,908 --> 00:28:58,975
You see, he said, I'm a Muslim.

401
00:28:59,620 --> 00:29:01,010
What did Rasool Allah tell him.

402
00:29:01,458 --> 00:29:07,154
قَالَ :لَوْ قُلْتَهَا وَأَنْتَ تَمْلِكُ أَمْرَكْ ، أَفْلَحْتَ كُلَّ الفَلَاحْ

403
00:29:08,167 --> 00:29:10,217
He told them, if you said it.

404
00:29:10,747 --> 00:29:12,053
وَأَنْتَ تَمْلِكُ أَمْرَكْ

405
00:29:12,107 --> 00:29:16,842
When you had the authority over yourself, then you would have been very successful.

406
00:29:17,396 --> 00:29:20,170
Meaning if you have said so when you were free

407
00:29:21,244 --> 00:29:28,170
now you are a captive and you're trying to claim that you are Muslim, this would have benefited you before.

408
00:29:29,352 --> 00:29:29,977
The man said:

409
00:29:30,017 --> 00:29:34,786
 يا محمد ، إِنِّيْ جَائِعٌ فَأَطْعِمْنِيْ وَإِنِّيْ ظَمْآنٌ فَاسْقِنِيْ

410
00:29:34,901 --> 00:29:40,143
He said: O Muhammad(محمد) I am hungry so feed me and I'm thirsty, so quench my thirst.

411
00:29:40,464 --> 00:29:41,666
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him;

412
00:29:41,706 --> 00:29:42,497
 هَذِه حَاجَتِكْ

413
00:29:42,577 --> 00:29:43,811
This is your need.

414
00:29:44,040 --> 00:29:51,180
In this regard, there are rights for the prisoner he's fed and he's provided for.

415
00:29:51,260 --> 00:29:54,601
 So Rasool Allah ﷺ told him this is your need, to take, what you need.

416
00:29:55,514 --> 00:29:59,506
Back we have stories in the Battle of Badr(بدر)  that the Ansaarرضي الله عنهم,

417
00:29:59,546 --> 00:30:03,333
when Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Treat the prisoners well.

418
00:30:03,701 --> 00:30:09,622
The Ansaar(انصار) would give the prisoners who are Mushrikeen(مشركين) from Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

419
00:30:09,793 --> 00:30:14,917
who came out to fight against Rasool Allah ﷺ they would give them the wheat bread

420
00:30:15,080 --> 00:30:20,404
and they, the Ansaar(أنْصَار) would eat the dates and it's considered that wheat bread is a better quality food.

421
00:30:20,949 --> 00:30:25,702
So, they would give them the bread and they would keep the dates for themselves.

422
00:30:26,535 --> 00:30:30,485
So now Rasool Allah ﷺ told him this is your need, we're not going to prevent you from eating and drinking.

423
00:30:31,780 --> 00:30:32,722
What happened next.

424
00:30:32,836 --> 00:30:37,693
He was used as a ransom for the two Muslims, who were taken prisoner.

425
00:30:37,990 --> 00:30:40,485
However he was not given his Camel back.

426
00:30:40,558 --> 00:30:42,941
Rasool Allah ﷺ took that camel for himself.

427
00:30:43,525 --> 00:30:49,065
So this man from Bannu Aqeel(بنوعقيل) was used in this prisoner exchange.

428
00:30:49,552 --> 00:30:52,030
He was exchanged for the two Muslim prisoners

429
00:30:52,354 --> 00:30:55,139
and Rasool Allah took Al-Adhba'a(ألعضباء) for himself

430
00:30:55,742 --> 00:31:00,014
and it was a very fast and good camel.

431
00:31:01,346 --> 00:31:07,927
Now, when the Mushrikeen(مشركين) have taken over camels of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

432
00:31:08,510 --> 00:31:14,733
they have also taken with them a Muslim woman from Bannu Ghaffar(بنوغفار)

433
00:31:15,244 --> 00:31:21,140
and whenever they would rest at night they would leave their camels.

434
00:31:21,380 --> 00:31:22,585
فِيْ اَفْنِيَتِهِمْ

435
00:31:22,625 --> 00:31:25,260
In their and this area with them.

436
00:31:25,806 --> 00:31:28,946
So this woman, one night while they were asleep

437
00:31:29,323 --> 00:31:37,092
she started walking towards each camel in order to take it and run away on its back to Madina

438
00:31:37,432 --> 00:31:39,935
but the camel would refuse, Ragha(رغا)

439
00:31:40,026 --> 00:31:46,020
it would make this sound, that the camel makes and until she came to Al-Adhba'a(ألعضباء)

440
00:31:46,060 --> 00:31:50,007
 and Al-Adhba'a(ألعضباء) was silent and when she rode on Al-Adhba'a(ألعضباء).

441
00:31:50,065 --> 00:31:50,862
 It was a very

442
00:31:51,365 --> 00:31:53,491
فَكَانَتْ نَاقَةْ ذَلُوْل

443
00:31:53,940 --> 00:31:59,699
it was very well domesticated and very simple to lead.

444
00:32:00,378 --> 00:32:07,990
So, she made Nadhar(نذر) a promise to Allah(عَزّوجَلّ), if Allah saves her on the back of this camel.

445
00:32:08,277 --> 00:32:10,618
She would slaughter this camel for the sake of Allah.

446
00:32:10,935 --> 00:32:12,577
So look at what her promise is.

447
00:32:12,853 --> 00:32:19,386
That this camel that will save her, if she arrives safely to Madina, she would slaughter this camel for the sake of Allah.

448
00:32:19,611 --> 00:32:25,891
 Now she did arrive to Madina and she told Rasool Allah ﷺ about her promise.

449
00:32:26,105 --> 00:32:27,475
Rasool Allah ﷺ told her.

450
00:32:27,546 --> 00:32:28,894
بِئْسِ مَا جَزِتِهَا

451
00:32:29,349 --> 00:32:33,503
What a bad reward you are rewarding this camel.

452
00:32:34,083 --> 00:32:38,831
This camel has saved you and brought you to Madina, now you want to slaughter it,

453
00:32:38,911 --> 00:32:40,826
and then Rasool Allah ﷺ told her.

454
00:32:41,100 --> 00:32:44,890
" لَا وَفَاءْ لِنَذْرٍ فِيْ مَعْصِيَةِ الله ، وَلَا فِيْمَا لِا يَمْلِكْ اِبْنِ آدَمْ "

455
00:32:45,345 --> 00:32:49,356
You do not have to fulfill a promise that includes a sin

456
00:32:49,615 --> 00:32:53,140
and you do not have to fulfill a promise

457
00:32:53,306 --> 00:32:56,485
and we're talking about Nadhar(نذر) here not promise with a human being.

458
00:32:56,742 --> 00:33:01,014
If you make Nadhar(نذر) to Allah, promise to Allah also if you don't own a thing

459
00:33:01,530 --> 00:33:05,398
and because he didn't own this camel, this camel belong to Rasool Allah ﷺ

460
00:33:05,683 --> 00:33:08,409
Rasool Ullah told her: Not to sacrifice the camel.

461
00:33:08,885 --> 00:33:09,276
Tayyab(طيب).

462
00:33:09,498 --> 00:33:14,604
Some lessons from these stories that we mentioned so far

463
00:33:15,071 --> 00:33:22,234
First of all in the Ghazwa(غزوة) of Zee Qarad(زي قرد)  we can see the fitness of Salama Bin Aqwa رضي الله عنه

464
00:33:22,544 --> 00:33:28,387
and we can see some of the activities that the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم would practice such as running,

465
00:33:28,863 --> 00:33:33,077
 Salamah(سلمه) and this man from Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار) they had the competition in running

466
00:33:33,117 --> 00:33:35,996
and that was approved by Rasool Allah ﷺ.

467
00:33:36,320 --> 00:33:40,293
So the Sahaba رضي الله عنهم were fit and they were strong

468
00:33:40,605 --> 00:33:45,630
and this is part of Edaad(ألعِدَاد) which the Muslims were commanded to do.

469
00:33:45,717 --> 00:33:50,363
The Muslims were told to prepare for the sake of Allahعَزّوجَلّ Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

470
00:33:50,943 --> 00:33:58,700
We can see here that Salama Bin Aqwa رضي الله عنه was pursuing this enemy for an entire day, without tiring out.

471
00:33:58,959 --> 00:34:02,572
In fact, they were getting tired and their beasts were getting tired

472
00:34:03,157 --> 00:34:07,805
because as we mentioned it, in the end of the Hadith(حديث) that they have left behind them two horses.

473
00:34:07,946 --> 00:34:09,473
 Why did they leave behind those two horses?

474
00:34:09,706 --> 00:34:10,737
Do you think about that?

475
00:34:11,164 --> 00:34:18,442
Why would they leave behind them two horses and a horse is a very valuable thing in those days, really expensive.

476
00:34:18,659 --> 00:34:21,584
 Why would they leave behind a horse, unless they had to?

477
00:34:21,692 --> 00:34:24,929
 Because the horse was tired, the horse was tired out.

478
00:34:25,214 --> 00:34:27,709
So they had to leave these two horses behind them.

479
00:34:28,209 --> 00:34:32,976
Salama Bin Aqwa(سلمه ابن اَلْاَكوع) was a very fit Sahabi رضي الله عنه.

480
00:34:34,250 --> 00:34:39,720
From the story of the woman, there's a lesson mentioned by An-Nawwawi(النووي)

481
00:34:40,032 --> 00:34:44,304
and this is regarding the traveling of a woman alone.

482
00:34:44,759 --> 00:34:47,030
يَقُوْلُ اَلنَّوَوِيْ فِيْ هَذَالْحَدِيْثْ

483
00:34:47,597 --> 00:34:52,597
جَوَازُ سَفَرِ الْمرأْة وَحْدَهَا بِلَا زَوْجَ وَلَا مَحْرَمْ

484
00:34:53,288 --> 00:34:56,895
وَلَا غَيْرَهُمَا اِذَا كَا نَ السَفَرَ ضَرُوْرة

485
00:34:57,454 --> 00:35:02,948
اِذَا كَانَ السَفَرَ ضَرُوْرَة، كَلْ هِجْرَهْ دَارِالحَرْبِ اِلَى دَارِ الْاِسْلَامْ

486
00:35:03,326 --> 00:35:07,546
وَ كَا الحَرَبِ مِمَّنْ يُرِيْدُ مِنْهَا فَاحِشَةً وَ نَحْوِيْ ذَالِكْ

487
00:35:08,144 --> 00:35:12,794
وَالنَّهِيْ عَنْ سَفَرِهَا وَحْدَهَا مَحْمُوْلٌ عَلَى غَيْرِ الضَّرُوْرَة

488
00:35:13,183 --> 00:35:19,769
He says in this Hadith(حديث), we can derive the ruling that it is allowed for a Muslim woman,

489
00:35:19,871 --> 00:35:27,613
 to travel alone without her husband or without a guardian and without anyone else.

490
00:35:28,184 --> 00:35:34,329
 If, it is a necessary travel and this is an important point that he mentions

491
00:35:34,637 --> 00:35:38,822
such as Hijrah(هجرة) from the land of war to the land of Islam.

492
00:35:39,459 --> 00:35:49,132
And such as running away from those who want to sin with her and similar situations

493
00:35:49,901 --> 00:35:58,644
and a Muslim woman is prohibited from traveling alone when there is no necessity in her travel.

494
00:35:59,180 --> 00:36:07,893
So, this would clarify some issues, here the statement by Imam An-Nawwawi رضي الله عنه

495
00:36:08,404 --> 00:36:12,126
clarifies this issue of the traveling a woman.

496
00:36:12,443 --> 00:36:19,559
Sometimes a Muslim woman is in great need of traveling alone and it's a necessity for her.

497
00:36:19,826 --> 00:36:26,075
 In this case she is allowed to and he mentions as an example, making Hijrah(هجرة).

498
00:36:26,764 --> 00:36:34,866
Tayyab(طيب) it's also probably beneficial here to talk about the rulings regarding POW's in general

499
00:36:34,974 --> 00:36:45,552
because we have covered a few cases up until this moment of how Muslims treat the POW's.

500
00:36:45,685 --> 00:36:51,895
 So we'll summarize it all now because we are already talking about prisoners that were taken in Al-Badr(البدر)

501
00:36:52,261 --> 00:36:55,595
and here we talked about this man from Banni Aqeel(بني عقيل).

502
00:36:55,997 --> 00:36:58,902
What is the ruling regarding prisoners of war?

503
00:36:59,448 --> 00:37:02,783
Can they be executed, can they be ransomed

504
00:37:03,146 --> 00:37:06,917
or should they be released, what is it exactly?

505
00:37:07,012 --> 00:37:11,767
Because we have seen that they were treated differently in different situations.

506
00:37:12,547 --> 00:37:16,103
To summarize this point, Ash-Shoukani(الشوكاني) says,

507
00:37:16,467 --> 00:37:22,091
مَذْهَبُ الْجَمْهُوْرْ اَنَّ الْاَمْرَ فِى الْاَسَارَى اَلْكَفَرة مِنْ الرِّجَالْ اِلَى الْاِمَامْ

508
00:37:22,470 --> 00:37:25,301
يَفْعَلُ مَاهُوَ أحظ لِلاِسْلَامِ وَ المُسْلِمِيْنْ

509
00:37:25,726 --> 00:37:33,145
He said, That the Mad'hab(مذهب) of the majority of scholars is that the issue of

510
00:37:33,578 --> 00:37:37,286
disbelieving prisoners of war is up to the Imam(اِمَام).

511
00:37:38,063 --> 00:37:44,458
The men, who are Kuffar(كفار) who are prisoners of war, it is up to the Imam(امام) to do with them

512
00:37:44,766 --> 00:37:48,192
what is the most beneficial for the Muslims.

513
00:37:48,313 --> 00:37:49,352
So, what does this mean?

514
00:37:49,657 --> 00:37:51,313
It means that Number one.

515
00:37:51,521 --> 00:37:55,496
They could be released without any compensation

516
00:37:56,123 --> 00:38:01,860
and the example of this is what Rasool Allah ﷺ did with Abu Azzah(ابوعزة) in the Battle of Badr(بدر).

517
00:38:02,169 --> 00:38:07,310
Abu Azzah(ابوعزة) was one of the captives the 70 captives that were taken in the battle of Badr(بدر).

518
00:38:07,887 --> 00:38:12,441
Abu Azzah(ابوعزة), he pleaded to the Messenger of Allah and told him that I have daughters

519
00:38:12,939 --> 00:38:16,392
that are left alone and I don't have any wealth to ransom myself.

520
00:38:16,857 --> 00:38:22,685
So for the sake of my daughters release me and Rasool Allah ﷺ released him,

521
00:38:23,248 --> 00:38:26,377
without asking him for any compensation whatsoever.

522
00:38:26,701 --> 00:38:30,580
He was only released on condition that he doesn't fight against the Muslims again

523
00:38:31,206 --> 00:38:33,111
and he consented to that.

524
00:38:33,711 --> 00:38:37,836
 The second option is to ransom them.

525
00:38:38,197 --> 00:38:43,782
And this is what happened with the rest of the prisoners in the Battle of Badr(بدر)

526
00:38:44,178 --> 00:38:49,306
such as Al-Abbas(العباس) they had to pay for their ransom and they were released.

527
00:38:49,646 --> 00:38:54,162
The third option they could be exchanged for Muslim prisoners.

528
00:38:54,470 --> 00:38:57,302
And the example of that is what we just talked about

529
00:38:57,834 --> 00:39:03,697
with this man from Banni Aqeel(بني عقيل) he was exchanged for two Muslim prisoners.

530
00:39:04,412 --> 00:39:07,060
The next option is to be executed

531
00:39:07,568 --> 00:39:10,713
and this is what Rasool Allah ﷺ did with An-Nazr Bin Haris(النضربن الحارث)

532
00:39:11,147 --> 00:39:13,588
and Uqba Bin Abi Moayeet(عقبةبن ابي معيت) in the Battle of Badr(بدر)

533
00:39:13,990 --> 00:39:19,022
and Abu Azzah(ابوعزة) when he was arrested again in the battle of Uhud(أحَد).

534
00:39:19,188 --> 00:39:21,197
 When he was captured again in the Battle of Uhud(أحَد)

535
00:39:21,658 --> 00:39:24,984
he has already promised that is not going to fight against Rasool Allah ﷺ

536
00:39:25,024 --> 00:39:31,506
 and now he was caught fighting against the Muslims, so he was executed.

537
00:39:32,023 --> 00:39:37,121
And also the entire fighting force of Bannu Quraizah(بنوقريظة), the Jewish tribe

538
00:39:37,539 --> 00:39:41,247
Rasool Allah ﷺ ordered, that they be put to death.

539
00:39:42,071 --> 00:39:48,918
So these are the different options that the Imam(اِمَام) has regarding the Prisoners of War.

540
00:39:49,446 --> 00:39:56,868
Next اِنْ شاءالله تعالى we'll talk about the important event of Al-Hudaybiya(الحديبيه),

541
00:39:57,389 --> 00:39:59,928
 so we'll leave that until our next session.

542
00:40:00,062 --> 00:40:01,702
بِاِذْنِ الله عَزُّوجَل

543
00:40:02,028 --> 00:40:07,119
 صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرًا

544
00:40:07,478 --> 00:40:09,746
السلام عليكم ورحمة الله وبركاته

